\import{base-macros}
\title{Swizzling (GPU)}
\tag{transient}

\p{There are two types of swizzling: \em{xor swizzling} and \em{shift swizzling}.}
\figure{
\<html:img>[width]{80\%}[src]{\route-asset{assets/img/xor-swizzle.png}}{}
\figcaption{xor swizzling assuming there are only 4 banks (instead of 32). Orientation expresses logical layout, whereas label / color denote the corresponding physical bank.}
}
\p{If each warp is only #{4} threads, then we can see after \em{xor swizzling} there will be zero bank conflicts when a warp tries to read a column.}
